  "hypothesis": "A learnable native tokenless public-factual shared/private gate trained with an auxiliary credit signal derived ONLY from previously observed physically chosen actions and their consequences (not private changed-law labels) will improve new-context unfamiliar-rule decisions over the same architecture trained without credit and over the strongest frozen fixed-route and phase-only controls, while preserving unchanged-rule transfer and old-context recall.",
  "credit": {
    "source": "Public observed R85/R86/R88 role-probed support factors, chosen action, its factual signed return, and visible context assignment; no hidden truth/unchosen query outcomes, future feedback, evaluator law ID, changed-regime flag or heldout label.",
    "mechanism": "For each FIT world only, compute all-256-rule public Bayes marginal evidence of one shared Boolean rule versus two independent Boolean rules, using ONLY observed factual signs and role pattern addresses. Fixed likelihood P(sign matches law)=0.85, mismatch=.15, uniform 256-rule prior, balanced prior same/different. Probability of different rules is sigmoid(log_evidence_independent-log_evidence_shared), bounded to [0.05,0.95]. This value is an imperfect publicly grounded observational contradiction proxy, not privileged causal truth or known learned intelligence.",
    "training_use": "Auxiliary binary-cross-entropy on the trainable native gate for new-context (B) FIT queries only, weight=0.25 against equal-context factual return regression loss. Fully differentiable route score; no heldout credit supervision or evaluator label. Score and gate trained ONLY on public FIT observations, then sealed prospective UNIT_UNSEEN evaluation.",
    "failure_modes": "Sparse eight-address observations, role probe noise and action-conditioned reward sign may make public Bayes contradiction credit unreliable; report empirical advantage versus no-credit and permuted-credit controls, no post hoc threshold or target repair.",
    "strict_no_private_labels": true,
    "likelihood_match": 0.85,
    "likelihood_mismatch": 0.15,
    "change_prior": 0.5,
    "aux_weight": 0.25,
    "target_clamp_low": 0.05,
    "target_clamp_high": 0.95,
    "placebo_control": "Same FIT contradiction targets deterministically permuted among FIT episodes within each minibatch, preserving marginal target distribution but breaking world-specific evidence alignment; no access to truth labels.",
